cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "llm-reward-portfolio"
abstract: >-
  Agentic reward engineering with LLMs for risk-sensitive deep-RL portfolio
  allocation: an LLM designs the reward-function code for a fixed Stable-Baselines3
  SAC portfolio agent, and the experiment tests whether feeding its Eureka-style
  reflection loop multi-level tail-risk feedback (CVaR at several levels, left-tail
  mass, robust skew) beats feeding it a scalar performance number, at matched compute,
  against scalar/placebo/single-CVaR controls. Pre-registered, likely-null framed via
  Mayoian error-statistical severity, on a single survivorship-free point-in-time
  LSEG equity panel. MSc dissertation, UCL Institute of Finance and Technology.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Tamer
    family-names: Atesyakar
    affiliation: "University College London (UCL), Institute of Finance and Technology — MSc Banking & Digital Finance"
